    "applyUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/search/results/content/?keywords=Secure-by-design%20architecture",
    "body": "Many teams proudly say:\n“We have SAST, DAST, container scanning, and IaC scanning in our pipeline.”\nThat’s good.\nBut if security findings are ignored, exceptions are unmanaged, and developers don’t understand the risks, you’ve simply automated the generation of security reports.\nNot security.\nSuccessful DevSecOps programs focus on three things:\n• Secure-by-design architecture\n• Developer ownership of security outcomes\n• Automation that reduces risk without slowing delivery\nThe objective is not to find more vulnerabilities.\nThe objective is to prevent vulnerable code from reaching production in the first place.\nThe most mature teams don’t ask:\n“How many vulnerabilities did we detect?”\nThey ask:\n“Why were we able to create them?”\nThat’s where real DevSecOps begins.\n#DevSecOps #CyberSecurity #AppSec #CloudSecurity #PlatformEngineering #ShiftLeft #DevOps #SoftwareEngineering"
