    "applyUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/search/results/content/?keywords=For%20fast-moving%20engineering%20teams%2C%20that%20judgment%20matters.",
    "body": "DevSecOps hiring gets messy when teams reduce it to tools.\nA candidate can know CI/CD platforms, scanning tools, and pipeline gates without being the right person to make security work inside engineering flow.\nThe real signal is adoption.\nWhat did engineering teams actually use? What moved earlier in the process? What feedback became faster? What controls reduced risk without creating constant noise? What changed in how developers interacted with security?\nThat is where DevSecOps becomes meaningful.\nIt is not just security plus CI/CD terminology. It is security that understands delivery reality.\nA strong DevSecOps-oriented cloud security candidate knows when to block, when to warn, when to guide, and when to build a better default. They understand that a technically correct control can still fail if it creates too much friction.\nFor fast-moving engineering teams, that judgment matters.\n#"
