    "body": "There’s a strange pattern in DevOps hiring right now.\nThe stronger the market gets,\nthe more similar candidates look on paper.\nRemove the names\nmost CVs become interchangeable.\nSame tools.\nSame structure.\nSame language.\nAWS ✅ Kubernetes ✅ Docker ✅ Terraform ✅\nWhich means hiring decisions are no longer about what you use.\nThey’re about one thing:\nWho shows impact fastest.\nNot:\n“Managed CI/CD pipelines”\nBut:\n“Reduced deployment failures by 40% through CI/CD optimisation”\nNot:\n“Handled cloud infrastructure”\nBut:\n“Reduced infrastructure cost by 25% through optimisation”\nSame experience.\nDifferent signal.\nIn a market where everyone looks qualified,\nclarity becomes your only advantage.\nMost candidates aren’t rejected because they’re not good\nthey’re rejected because they’re indistinguishable.\nTools get you in the game.\nImpact decides if you’re chosen.\n#DevOps #CloudEngineering #TechHiring #Car"
