    "applyUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/search/results/content/?keywords=Promoting%20vs%20Looping%20in%20DevOps%20%E2%80%93%20Understanding%20the%20Difference",
    "body": "🚀 Promoting vs Looping in DevOps – Understanding the Difference\nWhile learning DevOps, I came across two important concepts: Promoting and Looping. Although they may seem similar, they serve different purposes in the software delivery process.\n📌 Promoting\n✅ Moves code through environments (Dev → Test → Staging → Production)\n✅ Linear and sequential process\n✅ Focuses on stability and release readiness\n✅ Used during deployments and releases\n📌 Looping\n✅ Repeats development and testing cycles in the same environment\n✅ Iterative and continuous process\n✅ Focuses on improvement and bug fixing\n✅ Common during development and testing phases\n💡 Simple Way to Remember:\n🔹 Promoting = Moving Forward\n🔹 Looping = Improving Before Moving Forward\nBoth are essential in DevOps:\n✔️ Loop to improve quality\n✔️ Promote when the code is ready\nEvery day I learn something new about DevOps, and understanding t"
