    "body": "🤣 JUST CHANGED ONE LINE IN DOCKERFILE...\nAs DevOps Engineers, we've all experienced this moment.\nYou make a tiny change, push the code, watch the pipeline turn green, and think:\n\"Looks good. Let's deploy.\" 😎\nA few minutes later:\n🔥 Production issues start appearing\n📞 Alerts begin flooding in\n👨‍💻 Teams start asking questions\n☕ Coffee consumption increases dramatically\nAll because of a single line that seemed completely harmless.\nThis is why DevOps is not just about automation—it's about building reliable processes.\n✅ Version pinning over latest\n✅ Proper testing in staging\n✅ Automated quality gates\n✅ Rollback strategies\n✅ Change reviews\nThe biggest incidents often don't come from massive architecture changes.\nThey come from that one small change everyone thought was safe.\nOne line. Big impact. That's DevOps. 😂\nWhat's the smallest change you've seen cause the biggest outage?\n#DevOps #"
