    "body": "The deeper you go into DevOps in 2026, the more you realize:\nIt's all infrastructure for someone else's idea.\nThe pipeline you built at 2am?\nIt shipped a feature that a product manager had been waiting 6 months for.\nThe Kubernetes cluster you spent a week tuning?\nIt's running a model that a researcher spent 2 years training.\nThe alert you fine-tuned to reduce noise?\nIt gave an on-call engineer their first full night of sleep in a month.\nThe golden path you built on the internal platform?\nA new junior engineer deployed their first service on day 3 — without needing anyone's help.\nDevOps is invisible when it works.\nThat's not a failure of recognition.\nThat's the point.\nThe best infrastructure is the kind nobody thinks about.\nBuild the thing that lets everyone else build their thing.\nThat's the job. And it's a good one.\n#DevOps #PlatformEngineering #SRE #InfrastructureEngineering #DevOpsPhi"
