    "body": "🚀 Excited to share my latest backend project!\n💡 Problem Statement :\nTraditional UPI transactions require an active internet connection. In places like underground parking, remote areas, or disaster situations, digital payments cannot be processed because the sender's device cannot communicate with the bank.\n✅ Proposed Solution\nThis project simulates an Offline UPI Mesh Network, where an encrypted payment packet is relayed through nearby devices using a mesh network until a bridge device with internet connectivity uploads it to the backend for settlement.\nTo make this approach secure and reliable, the project addresses three important backend challenges:\n🔐 Hybrid Encryption (RSA + AES) – Ensures that intermediate devices carrying the packet cannot read or modify the payment details.\n🔄 Idempotency – Prevents duplicate settlements even if multiple bridge devices upload the same payment "
