    "body": "Day 1 of 21 – What a Business Analyst Actually Does (And What Most People Get Wrong)\nWhenever I tell someone I'm a Business Analyst, I usually hear one of these:\n❌ \"So you write requirement documents?\"\n❌ \"You're the person between the client and developers?\"\n❌ \"You spend most of your day in meetings?\"\nThose things are part of the role, but they don't define it.\nAt its core, a Business Analyst's job is to understand a business problem and make sure the team solves the right problem.\nLet me give you a simple example.\nA client says: \"Our restaurant staff are wasting too much food.\"\nA BA doesn't immediately jump into writing requirements.\nInstead, the questions start:\n• Where is the waste happening: during preparation, storage, or service?\n• Is this a process issue or a system issue?\n• How are we measuring waste today?\n• What would success actually look like?\nAfter digging deeper, the real r"
