    "body": "🚀 STM32 Peripheral Mastery Series – Day 7/10: I²C (Inter-Integrated Circuit) 🔗\nSo far, we've learned how STM32 interacts with hardware using GPIO, responds to events with EXTI, manages time using Timers, communicates through UART, converts analog signals using ADC, and transfers high-speed data using SPI.\nToday, let's explore one of the most widely used communication protocols in embedded systems: I²C.\nUnlike SPI, where every device typically requires its own Chip Select line, I²C allows multiple devices to communicate using just two wires.\n⚡ Why I²C?\nImagine building an IoT weather station.\nYou need to connect:\n🔹 Temperature Sensor\n🔹 Pressure Sensor\n🔹 RTC Module\n🔹 EEPROM\n🔹 OLED Display\nInstead of dedicating separate communication lines to every peripheral, I²C lets all these devices share the same bus, making hardware design much simpler and more scalable.\nThe secret?\n👉 Every de"
