    "body": "🚀 As part of #ICOP QEC #EtherCAT Solutions portfolio, we are sharing a practical system architecture for integrating #Python-based applications with real-time EtherCAT #motion control over Ethernet.\nIntegrating higher-level software with EtherCAT motion control is often more challenging than the motion control itself.\nThis architecture demonstrates how a Python application communicates over standard Ethernet, while QEC-M-01 handles deterministic EtherCAT motion control in the real-time domain.\n👉 Explore the full tutorial:\nhttps://lnkd.in/gYjvxgz5\n🌐 Key Concept\nInstead of requiring a PC-side EtherCAT stack, the system enables:\n🧩 Python to focus on application logic\n🧩 QEC-M-01 to handle real-time EtherCAT control\n🧩 Standard Ethernet as the communication bridge\n🧠 Engineering Value\nThis decoupled architecture helps engineers:\n• Reduce system complexity on the PC side\n• Maintain determ"
