    "body": "Remote Terminal Unit (RTU)\nIn industrial automation and SCADA systems, the Remote Terminal Unit (RTU) plays a critical role in monitoring, data acquisition, and control. A typical RTU consists of several key hardware components designed to ensure reliability, accuracy, and continuous operation.\nControl Processor (CPU)\nThe RTU is generally built around a 16-bit or 32-bit microprocessor, such as the Motorola 68302 or Intel 80386. The processor manages data collection, communication, and control functions.\nMemory Architecture\nA typical RTU memory configuration may include:\nEPROM (or Battery-Backed RAM) – 256 kB\nUsed for storing firmware and critical system programs.\nRAM – 640 kB\nProvides temporary storage for operational data and processing tasks.\nFlash Memory / EEPROM – 128 kB\nAllows non-volatile storage of configuration settings and application data.\nThe total memory capacity can be expan"
