    "applyUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/search/results/content/?keywords=What%20is%20an%20Engineer%3F",
    "body": "What is an Engineer?\nTo me, an engineer is someone who understands, controls, modifies, and designs systems.\nThe only thing that changes is the system.\n⚙️ Mechanical Systems → Mechanical Engineering\n⚡ Electrical Systems → Electrical Engineering\n🏭 Industrial Systems → Industrial Engineering\nNow here’s where it gets interesting.\nIndustrial systems are rarely simple.\nThey involve multiple interconnected elements:\n• Processes\n• Manufacturing\n• Automation\n• Quality & Regulatory Controls\n• Human Factors\n• Human Resources\n• Data, Planning, and much more\nThat’s what makes Industrial Engineering unique.\nAn Industrial Engineer doesn’t just focus on one machine or one function.\nWe look at the entire system.\nWe connect people, processes, machines, materials, and data to make everything work better.\nThat’s why a great Industrial Engineer often becomes:\nA Jack of all trades\nor\nA Master of one domain "
