    "body": "I thought data analysis was just Excel formulas... until today’s lesson called me a DOCTOR 🤯\nDay 1 of relearning data.\nI sat down expecting formulas. Instead, the lesson said:\n“A data analyst is like a doctor for data.”\n•Examining: Checking the data for problems (like checking a patient for symptoms)\n•Cleaning: Removing the “disease” (errors and duplicates)\n•Transforming: Making the data healthy\n•Interpreting: Explaining it to stakeholders using visuals, because they don't always understand raw numbers.\nThen my brain broke 🤔:\n*Data ≠ Information ≠ Insight*\n•Data: Raw facts. E.g., “20, 23, 26, 30”\n•Information: Processed data. E.g., “Ages of people who purchased our products”\n•Insight: The deep understanding that drives action. E.g., “Most buyers are aged 20–30, so let’s market youth products.”\n😌 4 takeaways from Day 1 — screenshot this:\n👉 *Lesson 1: The 4 types of analytics\n• Descrip"
